    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n### The Problem\nWhen running `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the root command's parser and not passed through to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. This prevented the workflow file from being created.\n\n### The Solution\nI made two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the root program** (line 604) - This allows subcommands to handle options independently\n2. **Added `.passThroughOptions()` to the gate command** (line 622) - This tells commander to pass through all options (including `--ci`) to the frai-gate process as arguments\n\n### Verification\nThe fix has been tested and confirmed:\n- \u2713 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n- \u2713 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is created  \n- \u2713 No errors appear\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready to use.",
